# ESP32 Pin Allocation & Hardware Mapping

This document outlines the pin configurations, functional roles, electrical characteristics, and hardware design considerations for the Motor Edge Guard system on the 30-pin ESP32 Dev Module.

---

## Pin Allocation Summary

| ESP32 Pin | Functional Name | Direction | Connected Device | Electrical Properties |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **GPIO 34** | `SENSOR_PIN` | Input | LM358 Output / SCT-013 | ADC1 Channel 6, 12-Bit (0-3.3V range), Input-only |
| **GPIO 13** | `RELAY_PIN` | Output | Solid-State Relay (SSR) | Digital Output, Active-HIGH trigger, 3.3V logic |
| **GPIO 4** | `RESET_BTN` | Input | Tactile Push Button | Digital Input, Configured with `INPUT_PULLUP` (Active-LOW) |
| **3V3** | Power Rail | Output | LM358 VCC | Regulated 3.3V rail from on-board LDO |
| **VIN / 5V**| Power Rail | Input/Output| Relay Board VCC | System 5V input rail from USB / external supply |
| **GND** | Ground Rail | Reference | All Components | Common system ground reference |

